This npm package (@rlwj-lab/opsxdb-mcp) is a Node launcher for the OpsxDB
MCP server (stdio). The real server is a Go binary named opsxdb-mcp.

Build it from the opsxdb repo:

  cd server && go build -o ../bin/opsxdb-mcp ./cmd/opsxdb-mcp

Then either:
  - put that binary on your PATH (ahead of any npm shim), or
  - export OPSXDB_MCP_BIN=/absolute/path/to/opsxdb-mcp

Cursor / Claude Desktop example:

  {
    "mcpServers": {
      "opsxdb": {
        "command": "npx",
        "args": ["-y", "@rlwj-lab/opsxdb-mcp"],
        "env": {
          "OPSXDB_MCP_BIN": "/absolute/path/to/opsxdb-mcp"
        }
      }
    }
  }

Config files (same as native binary):
  ~/.opsxdb/mcp.json
  ~/.opsxdb/connections.json
